  "beats": [
    {
      "t": "2026-11-18T00:00:01Z",
      "text": "Ukrainian forces struck the Crimean Bridge for the third time in four days, and Russian authorities then closed the bridge to all traffic.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:2026-11-18:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-18T00:00:08Z",
      "text": "The first attack, on 16 November 2026, shifted one of the road bridge's structural arches by about 15 degrees, according to Russian media, and led to a partial closure of road traffic.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1386578878:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-18T00:00:15Z",
      "text": "Starting on 16 November 2026, as part of the Russo-Ukrainian war, Ukrainian forces repeatedly targeted the bridge with missiles and drones, causing severe damage and stopping traffic again and again.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1386578878:0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-18T00:00:25Z",
      "text": "The reports place Ukraine as the country whose forces carried out the strikes on the bridge.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:2026-11-18:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-18T00:00:33Z",
      "text": "The reports also name the Crimean Bridge, the structure at the center of these attacks.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:2026-11-18:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-18T00:00:42Z",
      "text": "The story is reported by AP and The Guardian.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:2026-11-18:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-18T00:00:50Z",
      "text": "NPR headlined its story 'Putin to meet with Trump and Xi after Ukrainian attack on Russian bridge.'",
      "cites": [
        "news:npr:e47dadc6bc04"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-18T00:00:56Z",
      "text": "DW headlined its piece 'What the Crimean bridge attack means for Russia.'",
      "cites": [
        "news:dw:1ee630640446"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-18T00:01:02Z",
      "text": "BBC News headlined its report 'New video shows explosions moments before part of Crimea Bridge collapses.'",
      "cites": [
        "news:bbc:e12a3e473d31"
      ]
    },
